(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-mystery-02","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"seventh-wharf","cn":["河灯节的[[ritual|仪式]]尚未结束，老陈带我们留在有巡查员的堤上。祠堂门前，老人和孩子低声[[chant|吟唱]]送灯歌，把纸船依次放入江流。热闹的[[ceremony|典礼]]散场后，伞沿滴水的声音都能听清。那阵突然的[[stillness|寂静]]里，B库方向传来拖动铁链的响声。程雾只戴一边耳机，另一边听我们说话，随后把录音时间记在本子上。","沿着公共步道走到库墙外，我们看见一串湿[[footprint|脚印]]，到墙脚便断了。糖画摊的女人说，去年也有人在这里‘穿墙’。程雾蹲下照相，每个鞋印边缘都有蓝色[[stain|污渍]]，干处留下的粉末呈颗粒状，[[texture|质地]]不像河泥。墙是新补的[[concrete|混凝土]]，没有能让人通过的洞；横向排水槽却接在最后一个脚印旁，槽底的水漫过了一段鞋痕。老陈没有碰粉末，只让我们把槽的走向拍全。","手机灯扫到槽内一条黑[[cable|电缆]]，它穿过通风口，末端被松木板[[concealed|遮藏]]着。钟声再响时，木板后也轻轻震动。程雾退回步道，说那里可能藏着播放声音的[[device|装置]]。至少这部分怪声是[[artificial|人为的]]，不必先找一个敲钟的人。摊主追问是谁骗她，程雾摇头：我们看见的是线和震动，还没看见安装的人。老陈立即拨通何警官的电话。","何警官接收照片，又请人调出堤口的[[surveillance|监控]]。录音里的钟在九点十九分响，九点十七分，一个雨衣人仍站在库墙边。两分钟的[[interval|间隔]]不能说明他就是赵启，却能[[contradict|反驳]]秦衡对巡查员说的‘这里三天没人靠近’。更[[suspicious|可疑的]]是，雨衣人没有沿河离去，而是拐向老街快印社。帽檐遮住了脸，我把视频放大，仍只得到模糊的色块。程雾让我停下，保存原画面。","第二天上午，巡查员陪我们[[inspect|检查]]外围。门上的纸[[seal|封条]]没破，墙后却能够到通风口。槽边有一片带蓝字的[[scrap|碎纸]]，背面印着档案页码格，正面只剩‘转存’二字；巡查员用夹子收进袋子。何警官把库后排水线与通往印刷店的[[route|路线]]一起标在图上。我盯着那片纸，第一次觉得父亲的船票不只指向旧河湾，还指向一个活人不愿我们找到的工作地点。"],"en":["The festival [[ritual|ritual]] was not over, so Chen kept us on the embankment where patrol staff were present. Outside the temple, adults and children began to [[chant|chant]] the lantern song and place their paper boats in the river. When the lively [[ceremony|ceremony]] ended, we could hear water dripping from umbrellas. In that sudden [[stillness|stillness]], a chain scraped somewhere toward warehouse B. Cheng wore only one earphone, leaving the other ear free to hear us. She wrote the recording time in her notebook.","Following the public path to the warehouse wall, we found a wet [[footprint|footprint]] trail that stopped at its base. A woman selling sugar figures said someone had 'walked through the wall' there the previous year. Cheng crouched to photograph it. Each print carried a blue [[stain|stain]] along its edge. Where it had dried, the powder had a grainy [[texture|texture]], unlike river mud. The wall was newly patched [[concrete|concrete]], with no opening large enough for a person. A drain ran sideways beside the last print, however, and water had covered part of the trail. Chen left the powder untouched and asked us to photograph the drain's whole course.","A phone light revealed a black [[cable|cable]] inside the drain. It passed through a vent, with its end [[concealed|concealed]] behind a loose board. When the bells sounded again, the board trembled slightly. Cheng stepped back onto the path. A [[device|device]] for playing sound might be hidden there, she said. At least part of the strange noise was [[artificial|artificial]]; we did not first have to find someone striking a bell. The seller demanded to know who had deceived her. Cheng shook her head. We had seen a wire and movement, not the person who installed them. Chen called Officer He immediately.","Officer He received our photographs and obtained the embankment [[surveillance|surveillance]] footage. The recorded bells sounded at 9:19; at 9:17, a person in a raincoat was still beside the warehouse. That two-minute [[interval|interval]] could not identify Zhao, but it could [[contradict|contradict]] Qin's claim to a patrol officer that nobody had approached for three days. More [[suspicious|suspicious]] was the person's departure toward the old street's printing shop rather than along the river. The hat hid the face. Enlarging the video gave me only blurred blocks of colour. Cheng asked me to stop and keep the original footage.","The next morning, a patrol officer accompanied us to [[inspect|inspect]] the outside. The paper [[seal|seal]] on the door was unbroken, but the vent could be reached from behind. A [[scrap|scrap]] of paper with blue lettering lay beside the drain. Its back carried an archive page-number grid; only the words 'transferred for storage' remained on the front. The officer collected it with forceps. Officer He marked both the rear drain and the [[route|route]] toward the printing shop on a map. Looking at the scrap, I first felt that Dad's ticket pointed beyond the old river bend, toward a living person's hidden work."]});
